WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:06.429
Hello and welcome to this video on dynamic nav meshes.

2
00:00:07.519 --> 00:00:11.759
Now, there may be times when you will need your nav mesh to update,

3
00:00:11.759 --> 00:00:14.880
and this is not done by default.

4
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.519
And I'm going to demonstrate that by...

5
00:00:18.879 --> 00:00:23.070
I'm going to grab this blue cube over here,

6
00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:27.890
drag this over, and I'm going to make a couple of changes to it.

7
00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:31.570
The first thing is I don't want to simulate physics for this one,

8
00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:35.409
I'm going to reduce the rotation so that it's flat.

9
00:00:36.799 --> 00:00:43.039
And I'm going to move this out so that it's a bit of a long one.

10
00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.899
Now, at the moment, you can see that this does not affect the navigation.

11
00:00:49.409 --> 00:00:55.890
And that is because for this, we have unticked the can ever affect navigation.

12
00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.820
If I take that on, you can see that's going to change it

13
00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:02.460
so the navigation is working around it.

14
00:01:04.609 --> 00:01:06.849
Now, I want this to move. So there's a couple of things.

15
00:01:06.849 --> 00:01:08.930
We're already movable, so that's fine.

16
00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:14.370
But I am going to add in a component just here.

17
00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:17.650
And this is going to be the rotating movement component.

18
00:01:18.849 --> 00:01:25.730
And the rotating movement is going to rotate on the z-axis by 180.

19
00:01:26.609 --> 00:01:29.569
And let's just try that one second.

20
00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.939
Yes, we can see that that's pretty fast.

21
00:01:34.939 --> 00:01:37.900
So we've got the rotation is moving pretty fast for that.

22
00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.060
I'm going to slow it down just a little bit.

23
00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:44.140
So I grab the rotating movement, I'm going to change that to 90.

24
00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.579
So that's about half the speed.

25
00:01:46.299 --> 00:01:50.859
Again, if I simulate, we can see that this is updating as we go.

26
00:01:51.739 --> 00:01:55.260
Now, what you'll notice here is as we're running,

27
00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.980
this isn't updating the nav mesh at all.

28
00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:01.420
So if I was to actually play when I was in the game,

29
00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:04.540
if I wanted to move to here, I could,

30
00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:10.259
but I can never cross this middle section because navigation is an update.

31
00:02:15.099 --> 00:02:17.099
Oh, this is quite easy to fix.

32
00:02:18.189 --> 00:02:22.270
Again, we have to jump into the project settings.

33
00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:28.189
So if we come up to the top, select project settings and navigation mesh here.

34
00:02:28.189 --> 00:02:32.349
So under navigation mesh, you'll see as we work our way through it,

35
00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:34.990
there is a runtime generation.

36
00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:40.800
So under generation, we have, I'm just going to search for it.

37
00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:46.050
Runtime goes to the top, here you go.

38
00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:49.729
Under the navigation mesh, we have the option for runtime generation.

39
00:02:50.849 --> 00:02:55.169
And if I drop this down, we have a couple of options.

40
00:02:55.169 --> 00:02:59.729
We have dynamic modifier only, and we have the dynamic.

41
00:02:59.729 --> 00:03:02.449
So we're going to use dynamic straight up.

42
00:03:03.009 --> 00:03:08.849
And now that that's ticked, if we simulate, you can see what's going on here.

43
00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:11.729
The nav mesh is updating as we go.

44
00:03:12.449 --> 00:03:19.490
Now you'll also be able to notice that the color of the sections

45
00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:24.849
that are now in red, these are the ones that have to update.

46
00:03:24.849 --> 00:03:29.169
To reduce the load runtime, you don't want to rebuild the entire nav mesh,

47
00:03:29.169 --> 00:03:30.689
especially if you've got quite a big level,

48
00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:33.490
that'd be very, very expensive for every moving object.

49
00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:42.060
So what it does is it will just rebuild the ones where something dynamic has moved in it.

50
00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:46.300
And if I reduced it and I could manage to fit it into a singular one,

51
00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:49.259
I'll just take that down to about four,

52
00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.699
you'll see that it's only going to affect this one.

53
00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:58.379
But it's in red because it needs to take time on tick to update this.

54
00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:04.909
OK, and as you probably noticed in the project settings,

55
00:04:04.909 --> 00:04:07.870
there was another option under runtime generation,

56
00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:11.310
and that is dynamic modifiers only.

57
00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:12.509
Let's select that.

58
00:04:13.789 --> 00:04:18.670
So you're in a situation where you do want the nav mesh to update,

59
00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.029
but not for every little thing.

60
00:04:20.589 --> 00:04:25.069
For example, these you could run through and knock them out the way.

61
00:04:25.069 --> 00:04:28.829
So if I was to show you at the moment when my character comes over,

62
00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:32.029
you might want to keep it so that they knock them out the way.

63
00:04:32.029 --> 00:04:36.110
And therefore, we wouldn't want these to affect the nav mesh,

64
00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.310
but we would want something like this to affect the nav mesh.

65
00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:43.550
So in this case, we can use modifiers only.

66
00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:47.470
So if I jump in to my project settings,

67
00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:50.110
change it to dynamic modifiers only,

68
00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:54.910
the first thing is when I play, you'll notice that nothing updates at all.

69
00:04:56.139 --> 00:05:01.899
Now what I'm going to do is I'm going to add another component

70
00:05:01.899 --> 00:05:03.819
to this rotating movement here,

71
00:05:04.379 --> 00:05:09.899
and I'm going to search for a nav modifier.

72
00:05:10.829 --> 00:05:13.629
OK, now you'd usually do this as part of a blueprint.

73
00:05:13.629 --> 00:05:16.189
So if you created a blueprint for something that revolves,

74
00:05:16.189 --> 00:05:19.149
you would add the modifier into the blueprint

75
00:05:19.149 --> 00:05:20.829
and it would be easier to manage.

76
00:05:20.829 --> 00:05:24.509
But I just want to get across in this demonstration how this works.

77
00:05:25.069 --> 00:05:30.029
Now I am going to change the extents to about 550

78
00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:32.189
so that it kind of matches what we've got there.

79
00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:35.069
And now if we look at that,

80
00:05:35.069 --> 00:05:41.149
you can see that this is updating as we would expect beforehand.

81
00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:45.230
Now there is one problem.

82
00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:48.350
The old nav mesh is below here.

83
00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:52.350
So we've already cut out this area.

84
00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.509
And because we're not taking it into consideration,

85
00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:58.430
that's going to stay there sort of indefinitely.

86
00:05:58.430 --> 00:05:59.550
So let's correct that.

87
00:06:00.189 --> 00:06:05.230
What I'm going to do is with the object selected under nav,

88
00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:08.029
I'm going to tick off Can Effect Navigation.

89
00:06:08.819 --> 00:06:11.060
So that means our nav modifier,

90
00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:13.540
which we won't see until we run the game,

91
00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:16.819
is the only thing which is going to affect this navigation.

92
00:06:16.819 --> 00:06:20.100
So if I run, you'll see that that opens.

93
00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:24.500
So that's a sort of opt-in effect.

94
00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:28.579
Navigation is only going to be affected by these nav modifiers.

95
00:06:28.579 --> 00:06:30.660
And these are something that you'd need to add

96
00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.220
to the things that you want to change the navigation.

97
00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:34.660
And you would need to...

98
00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:38.180
And it would update it accordingly.

99
00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:41.620
So that is the nav modifier.

100
00:06:43.699 --> 00:06:47.939
And that's the basics of the dynamic nav mesh.

101
00:06:48.579 --> 00:06:52.740
The next thing we'll be looking at is the nav mesh in the vocal.
